body:
This Dart function filters repeat barcode reads from a camera scanner in our warehouse app. It ignores a code if the same value was seen less than 1500 ms ago:

if (code == last && now.difference(lastAt) < gap) return;
last = code; lastAt = now;

I'm unsure about two things: should lastAt update when a repeat is ignored (otherwise a label held in front of the camera gets accepted again every 1.5 seconds), and is comparing only the string enough when two different cartons carry the same code? Please look at the timing logic.
